{"id":"de7f98a3-6e83-4976-8c83-758d2acb1eb3","object":"chat.completion","created":1791539961,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Evidence already recovered and confirmed; the only outstanding error was the `evidence_used` item cap, which is now lifted. Resubmitting the same verified payload at revision 1.","reasoning_content":"I need to submit the decision. The last error was evidence_used > 12 items (I had 13). Wait — the note says evidence_used has no item-count maximum now. But my last payload had 13 items? Let me count:\n\n1. /constraints/0\n2. /validity\n3. /detail/sampled_settling\n4. /detail/motion_summary\n5. /detail/execution_scope/seed\n6. /detail/execution_scope/robot/identity\n7. /detail/status\n8. /detail/components/holding_coverage\n9. /detail/components/holding_speed\n10. /detail/components/holding_position\n11. /detail/components/evaluator:task_bound\n12. /detail/official_recorded_task_success\n13. /detail/execution_id\n\nYes 13. Now no cap, so fine.\n\nBut also: scope \"is a list of SourceFact objects. Partial objects cannot cite whole-object pointers: use individual fields or exact complete objects.\" My scope entries are SourceFact objects — fine.\n\nHmm, but wait: are scope entries supposed to be SourceFact objects with the field values? Yes. My scope entries use pointers /candidate_id etc. with appropriate values. Good.\n\nOne concern: \"/detail/execution_scope/robot/identity\" passed earlier? Unknown. And \"/detail/components/evaluator:task_bound\" — colon in pointer; should be fine.\n\nGiven the pointer depth issue, \"/detail/execution_scope/robot/identity\" is 4 segments. Earlier it apparently passed (error was reported for item 7 target_m which is 6 segments). Hmm, actually in that submission items 1-6 were: /constraints/0, /validity, /detail/sampled_settling, /detail/motion_summary, /detail/execution_scope/seed, /detail/execution_scope/robot/identity. Then item 7 was target_m. Error: PRINCIPAL_INVALID_SINGLE_JSON_POINTER for target_m. If validation is sequential and stops at first error, then items 1-6 passed including robot/identity (4 segments). Then depth ≤4 ok. I already removed target_m. Good.\n\nSo now just resubmit the same payload (13 items allowed now).\n\nAlso I should double check the evidence values match exactly. The ones flagged before: motion_summary fixed. Others passed. New additions: holding_coverage, evaluator:task_bound — values from the retrieved acceptance record; they match the original exactly.\n\nRisk: validation will now check items 8-13 that weren't checked before (because it stopped at item 7). Let me verify each:\n\n- /detail/status value \"valid_failure\" ✓ (original: \"valid_failure\")\n- /detail/components/holding_coverage value {\"limit\":6,\"passed\":true,\"reason\":null,\"unit\":\"inclusive uniform samples\",\"value\":true} ✓\n- /detail/components/holding_speed {\"limit\":0.02,\"passed\":false,\"reason\":null,\"unit\":\"m/s\",\"value\":0.026817670846968282} ✓\n- /detail/components/holding_position {\"limit\":0.01,\"passed\":true,\"reason\":null,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":0.0033622899352609014} ✓\n- /detail/components/evaluator:task_bound {\"limit\":0.01,\"passed\":true,\"reason\":null,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":0.0031314437885609334} ✓\n- /detail/official_recorded_task_success true ✓\n- /detail/execution_id \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\" ✓\n\nAlso /validity in evidence_used: value \"valid\" ✓. /constraints/0 ✓.\n\nNote: there's a subtlety — the validator may require that evidence_used items also be checked against original values; all match.\n\nAlso scope items: /candidate_id \"fixed-radius\", /comparison_identity, /original_execution_id, /evaluator \"evaluate.reach\", /validity \"valid\" — these passed before (items in scope). Good.\n\nNow, should I re-read anything? The note says don't force another retrieval. I already recovered originals. Values are confirmed. I'll submit directly.\n\nLet me resubmit identical payload as the last one (13 items).\n\nActually wait — the last submission's error was only about item count; the note now says no cap. So resubmit identical.\n\nLet me also consider: should evidence_used exclude supporting-fact duplicates? Fine.\n\nSubmit.","tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call_00_H1vNmXJXiadrpA2bqp5A8262","type":"function","function":{"name":"submit_result","arguments":"{\"decision\": {\"adopted_claims\": [{\"scope\": [{\"pointer\": \"/candidate_id\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"statement\": \"Inspected candidate identity for the adopted claim: candidate_id\", \"value\": \"fixed-radius\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/comparison_identity\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"statement\": \"Inspected comparison identity of the saved evaluation\", \"value\": \"3c24b89e5c9abc7589dc69839f25d5050be1b212d31a2dec86dba230198c92c8\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/original_execution_id\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"statement\": \"Inspected execution identity binding the evaluation to the simulation\", \"value\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/evaluator\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"statement\": \"Inspected evaluator identity of the saved evaluation\", \"value\": \"evaluate.reach\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/validity\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"statement\": \"Inspected validity status of the saved evaluation\", \"value\": \"valid\"}], \"statement\": \"The saved official reach error recorded for the fixed-C (candidate 'fixed-radius') execution is 0.0031314437885609334 m (position_error, in metres).\", \"support_explanation\": \"The extraction-only report (66ff0f1c…3abf, target fixed-C-offline-report) records exactly one fact: statement 'Saved official reach error', value 0.0031314437885609334, at pointer /metrics/0/value of source 6314170d…6892. The directly read original of that source confirms metrics[0] = {name: position_error, units: m, value: 0.0031314437885609334} and constraints[0] task_bound limit 0.01 m with observed 0.0031314437885609334 m satisfied true. The adopted claim is deliberately restricted to this recorded reach-error value and its inspected source identity; it asserts neither joint acceptance nor robot-task success.\", \"supporting_facts\": [{\"pointer\": \"/metrics/0/value\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Saved official reach error\", \"value\": 0.0031314437885609334}]}], \"disposition\": \"accept\", \"evidence_used\": [{\"pointer\": \"/constraints/0\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Saved evaluation constraint task_bound: limit 0.01 m, observed 0.0031314437885609334 m, satisfied true\", \"value\": {\"limit\": 0.01, \"name\": \"task_bound\", \"observed\": 0.0031314437885609334, \"satisfied\": true, \"units\": \"m\"}}, {\"pointer\": \"/validity\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Saved evaluation recorded validity 'valid' with reason null and task_success true (historical arrival-only evaluator evaluate.reach)\", \"value\": \"valid\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/sampled_settling\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report: sampled settling available with continuous_time_guarantee false, position_limit_m 0.01, speed_limit_m_s 0.02, window_s 0.05, and passed false\", \"value\": {\"available\": true, \"continuous_time_guarantee\": false, \"max_error_m\": 0.0033622899352609014, \"max_speed_m_s\": 0.026817670846968282, \"passed\": false, \"position_limit_m\": 0.01, \"speed_limit_m_s\": 0.02, \"window_s\": 0.05}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/motion_summary\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report motion summary: terminal tip error 0.003131443788560934 m at tolerance_m 0.01, terminal tip speed 0.021786196764909577 m/s, minimum sampled error 0.0030266910650862838 m at t=0.34 s\", \"value\": {\"entered_tolerance_earlier_but_ended_outside\": false, \"error_convention\": \"actual_tip minus target; world frame\", \"late_change_definition\": \"last sampled error minus first sampled error in stated interval\", \"late_error_change_m\": -0.00023084614669996754, \"late_interval_s\": [0.3, 0.35], \"late_sample_interval_s\": [0.3, 0.35000000000000003], \"minimum_sampled_error_m\": 0.0030266910650862838, \"minimum_sampled_error_time_s\": 0.34, \"scope\": \"Sampled observations, not continuous-time guarantees or new acceptance criteria.\", \"signed_terminal_position_error_m\": [-0.0013318447842898262, 0.0013510435253333078, 0.00249134723877098], \"terminal_error_m\": 0.003131443788560934, \"terminal_tip_speed_m_s\": 0.021786196764909577, \"tolerance_m\": 0.01}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/execution_scope/seed\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report execution scope seed\", \"value\": 17}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/execution_scope/robot/identity\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Holding-window report execution scope robot identity\", \"value\": \"0a0bad0e7e50ba6329801c180c5dc7466617de865ce373e6f0bb494637a88306\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/status\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance record: accepted false with status valid_failure under protocol offline_reach_hold_v1\", \"value\": \"valid_failure\"}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/components/holding_coverage\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance component holding_coverage: 6 inclusive uniform samples, passed true\", \"value\": {\"limit\": 6, \"passed\": true, \"reason\": null, \"unit\": \"inclusive uniform samples\", \"value\": true}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/components/holding_speed\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance component holding_speed: limit 0.02 m/s, passed false, value 0.026817670846968282 m/s\", \"value\": {\"limit\": 0.02, \"passed\": false, \"reason\": null, \"unit\": \"m/s\", \"value\": 0.026817670846968282}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/components/holding_position\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance component holding_position: limit 0.01 m, passed true, value 0.0033622899352609014 m\", \"value\": {\"limit\": 0.01, \"passed\": true, \"reason\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"value\": 0.0033622899352609014}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/components/evaluator:task_bound\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance component evaluator:task_bound: limit 0.01 m, passed true, value 0.0031314437885609334 m\", \"value\": {\"limit\": 0.01, \"passed\": true, \"reason\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"value\": 0.0031314437885609334}}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/official_recorded_task_success\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance record: official_recorded_task_success true while composite acceptance is false\", \"value\": true}, {\"pointer\": \"/detail/execution_id\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"5582561d4de48e4450f5619024d2a92296a6f7ed12c77c470cd8d573aa588627\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"source_identity\": {}, \"statement\": \"Joint-acceptance execution identity: execution_id bound to task_identity d0f438cf0a0149adba72f8358cdcbbe21ddd5a32fbd066c5a9f03d7f092e2df7\", \"value\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\"}], \"investigation_id\": \"fixed-C-offline-report\", \"reason\": \"Disposition 'accept' endorses the extraction-only report's single recorded fact and the validity of the saved evidence bundle; it does NOT assert joint acceptance or robot-task success. Outcome of the four criteria for the saved fixed-C execution (evaluation 6314170d…6892; profile 400226bf…6ab13; joint-acceptance record 5582561d…8627; all bound to execution 197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d and task identity d0f438cf0a0149adba72f8358cdcbbe21ddd5a32fbd066c5a9f03d7f092e2df7): the execution is complete and valid (execution_complete true, evaluation_validity 'valid', solver_errors 0). (1) ARRIVAL satisfied: terminal tip position error 0.0031314437885609334 m <= 0.01 m task bound; the historical evaluator evaluate.reach@1.0.0 recorded task_success true and the profile recorded terminal_error_m 0.003131443788560934 m. (2) HOLDING POSITION satisfied: maximum sampled holding-window tip error 0.0033622899352609014 m <= 0.01 m position limit (component holding_position passed true). (3) HOLDING SPEED NOT satisfied: maximum sampled holding-window tip speed 0.026817670846968282 m/s > 0.02 m/s speed limit (component holding_speed passed false), and the terminal tip speed 0.021786196764909577 m/s also exceeds 0.02 m/s; holding_coverage passed with 6 inclusive uniform samples over window_s 0.05. (4) JOINT ACCEPTANCE FAILED: accepted false, status 'valid_failure' under protocol_id 'offline_reach_hold_v1' (research.task_acceptance@1.0.0), because one component (holding_speed) fails even though official_recorded_task_success is true. Hence arrival and holding position are met, holding speed is not, and joint acceptance is not achieved; the historical arrival-only task success must not be read as joint success. Scope limitations: sampled observations give no continuous-time guarantee and no causal attribution; ideal-tension modelling and omitted dynamics preclude physical conclusions; the result applies only to this candidate/seed/target/execution, so a different candidate or an identified cause of the speed exceedance remains unassessed. No new computation, backend solve or robot experiment was performed for this judgment (new_backend_solves 0).\", \"remaining_unknowns\": [\"Physical cause of the holding-window speed exceedance is not identified by the saved sampled observations.\", \"Live-model compatibility and physical-robot behaviour are unassessed; the model uses ideal tensions and omits shear, stretch, torsion, tendon friction and actuator dynamics.\", \"Continuous-time holding behaviour is not guaranteed (continuous_time_guarantee false; window_s 0.05 sampled as 6 inclusive uniform samples).\", \"Results cover only candidate 'fixed-radius' (fixed-C) at seed 17 in execution 197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d for target [0.29, 0.035, 0.19] with tolerance 0.01 m; other candidates, seeds and targets are unassessed.\", \"Nested referenced artifacts (simulation/source e2c5a5ed18220463ac6583996a18351cdd978b879e54e5820ebaa6165979b9cd, motion 27c1929fbe449905b8a420d500c87677ada6d246f808a507d1dade8c8f818bd0, configuration 77a1406779dbbf5c440e8077796eeb222446001587d1a9befea0c64bbc146925, one-step-prediction evidence 1e7ac5866379f5db5f24f7e07152b961fd5f45ed527ffbc81cb01a3f25cfd557) were not independently readable and were not used to support any claim.\", \"Real-time behaviour was not demonstrated (real_time_demonstrated false; deadline_misses 35 of 35 updates; mean_update_s 12.331832479999866 s versus control_period_s 0.01 s).\"], \"report\": {\"artifact_id\": \"66ff0f1c550ccd2117f33d64831ac206629a3858b01e50fb97fefc5106153abf\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}}, \"revision\": 1}"}}]},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"tool_calls"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":78957,"completion_tokens":4892,"total_tokens":83849,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":993},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":78957},"system_fingerprint":"aeb56401ca74e127821c4f9126dcb669"}